        "stdout": "code=0\ncode=1\nvisible\n",
        "stderr": "cat: -: Bad file descriptor\n"
      },
      "note": "bash accepts a standard descriptor opened in the other direction (pinned on 5.2): fd 0 for writing is write-only, so a read is EBADF; fd 1 or 2 for reading is read-only, so a write fails. In a subshell so the battery's shared session keeps its streams."
